{
  "dom_id": "step-138226",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Converting Right-Bounded Intervals to Inequalities",
  "problem": "What inequality corresponds to the interval $x\\in\\left(-\\infty, 9\\right)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The statement $x \\in \\left(-\\infty, 9\\right)$ means that $x$ lies between $-\\infty$ and $9,$ where \n\n- the left endpoint $-\\infty$ is *not* included, and\n\n- the right endpoint $9$ is *not* included.\n\nTherefore, the inequality represented by this interval is \n\n$$\n-\\infty <   x <   9.\n$$\n\nHowever, since all numbers are greater than negative infinity, it suffices to write \n\n$$\nx <   9.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
